              "excerpt": "If a timeout occurs, it cancels the task and raises TimeoutError.",
              "span": 231
            }
          ],
          "text": "When asyncio.wait_for times out, it cancels the awaited task and raises TimeoutError."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "fd644b0b41d94d9a50f396a2ea4da31f9314e47a3c7f7b0d9c0c40e28c8539a4",
              "excerpt": "The function will wait until the future is actually cancelled, so the total wait time may exceed the timeout. If an exception happens during cancellation, it is propagated.",
              "span": 233
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "fd644b0b41d94d9a50f396a2ea4da31f9314e47a3c7f7b0d9c0c40e28c8539a4",
              "excerpt": "Changed in version 3.7: When aw is cancelled due to a timeout, wait_for waits for aw to be cancelled. Previously, it raised TimeoutError immediately.",
              "span": 237
            }
          ],
          "text": "The total wait time may exceed the timeout because wait_for waits until the future is actually cancelled; if an exception happens during cancellation, it is propagated."
        }
      ],
